   "text": "telli took €13.1m in seed money led by redalpine, with Cherry Ventures and Y Combinator following on, taking a two-year-old Berlin company past €16m raised in total. Its founders are betting that customer operations are one system pretending to be five — calls, CRMs, tickets, dashboards, each with its own queue and its own manual work behind it — and that AI belongs in the middle of that, running the operation rather than summarising it afterwards. It is a fat, unglamorous target, and unglamorous B2B software sold to people with real operational pain is precisely what Germany has been quietly good at for a decade.",
